.Dd November 10, 2026
.Dt VKMS 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vkms
.Nd virtual kernel mode setting, a display in software
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cm rach2.vkms
.Op Cm vkms.enable_cursor Ns = Ns Ar bool
.Op Cm vkms.enable_overlay Ns = Ns Ar bool
.Pp
.In drm/drm.h
.In drm/drm_mode.h
.Pp
.Pa /dev/dri/cardN
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver is a display with no hardware behind it, as Linux 6.12's vkms is:
it takes commits, counts vblanks at the rate of the mode set, and composes
each frame in memory to give its CRC, so that IGT's tests of mode setting,
vblanks and CRCs run on a machine without a display.
It starts only when
.Cm rach2.vkms
is on the kernel command line, after the other display drivers, and binds
one device.
Linux's module parameters
.Cm vkms.enable_cursor ,
on by default, and
.Cm vkms.enable_overlay ,
off by default, choose its planes; a value of
.Ql y ,
.Ql Y ,
.Ql 1
or
.Ql on
is true and
.Ql n ,
.Ql N ,
.Ql 0
or
.Ql off
false.
.Pp
The device is a DRM device, as
.Xr drm 4
describes, registered as
.Ql vkms
with Linux's identity: description
.Ql Virtual Kernel Mode Setting ,
version 1.0.0 and date 20180514, on the platform bus as
.Pa /sys/devices/platform/vkms ,
whose GET_UNIQUE name is
.Ql vkms .
It has a card node alone, and the features
.Dv DRIVER_MODESET ,
.Dv DRIVER_ATOMIC
and
.Dv DRIVER_GEM .
Its dumb buffers are kept in memory and may be shared through PRIME.
The kernel logs
.Dq vkms: registered
with the number of planes and the card.
.Ss Display
The device has one CRTC, and planes in Linux's order, which is their order
from the bottom up: the primary, eight overlays with
.Cm vkms.enable_overlay ,
and the cursor unless
.Cm vkms.enable_cursor
is false.
Each plane takes ARGB8888, XRGB8888, XRGB16161616, ARGB16161616 and
RGB565, linear, has the
.Ql rotation
property with every rotation and reflection, and is placed anywhere on the
CRTC, clipped to it, but not scaled.
The CRTC has the
.Ql GAMMA_LUT
property, with
.Ql GAMMA_LUT_SIZE
256, and a legacy gamma table of 256 entries.
One encoder of type
.Dv DRM_MODE_ENCODER_VIRTUAL
drives one connector of type
.Dv DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_VIRTUAL ,
.Ql Virtual-1 ,
always connected, whose modes are the DMT modes up to 8192x8192 and 61 Hz,
with 1024x768 preferred.
Framebuffers are from 10x10 to 8192x8192 pixels, and a cursor up to
512x512.
.Pp
While a holder wants vblanks the CRTC counts one each frame of the mode
set, its pixels with blanking over its clock, from the kernel's tick; an
event or a wait for a vblank therefore comes up to a millisecond after
the frame ends.
A tick that comes more than eight frames late counts eight and starts
the frames again from then.
.Ss CRCs
The CRTC's one CRC source is
.Ql auto ,
with one value a frame.
While the source runs, each vblank asks the composer thread,
.Ql kvkms ,
for its frame: the planes the last commit showed, each pixel widened to 16
bits a channel, blended in order over opaque black as premultiplied
alpha, and passed through the gamma table, as Linux's vkms composes them.
The value is the CRC-32 of the frame's rows, pixel by pixel as four
little-endian 16-bit values, alpha, red, green and blue, with no
inversion, Linux's
.Fn crc32_le
from 0.
A composer that falls behind gives the frames it missed the CRC of the
frame it composed.
The same frame gives the same CRC; the values are not those Linux gives
for a rotated plane, whose composition this driver does not copy.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /dev/dri/cardN
.It Pa /dev/dri/cardN
The card node of the device.
.El
.Sh ERRORS
Besides those of
.Xr drm 4
and
.Xr drm-kms 7 :
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Er EINVAL
A commit whose
.Ql GAMMA_LUT
has more than 256 entries; a scaled plane; a CRC source other than
.Ql auto .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bochs 4 ,
.Xr drm 4 ,
.Xr fbdrm 4 ,
.Xr drm-kms 7
.Sh HISTORY
The driver follows Linux 6.12's vkms: its objects, limits, formats,
blending, gamma table, vblank timer and CRC source.
It has no writeback connector, which Linux's has unless
.Cm vkms.enable_writeback
is false.
